      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting a \"run-time error '1004': application-defined or object-defined error\" on this macro i wrote for my monthly reconciliation. it happens right when it tries to copy the range to the new sheet. can u see what's wrong?\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsSource As Worksheet\n    Dim wsDest As Worksheet\n    Set wsSource = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Data_Input\")\n    Set wsDest = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Report\")\n    \n    ' trying to copy the data range\n    wsSource.Range(\"A1:G500\").Copy Destination:=wsDest.Range(\"A1\")\n    \n    MsgBox \"Reconciliation Complete\"\nEnd Sub",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The error \"1004\" is a classic sign that Excel is having a moment, but in this case, it's almost certainly because the destination sheet named \"Recon_Report\" doesn't actually exist yet in your workbook. When you try to copy data to a sheet that isn't there, Excel throws a runtime error, and the macro stops before it can finish its job.\n\nTo fix this, you need to check if the sheet exists first, and if it doesn't, create it before attempting to copy the data. You can do this by checking the `Count` of sheets or using a `Select` statement to create a new one. Once the sheet is ready, the copy operation will work smoothly, and your reconciliation will run without any hiccups.\n\nHere is the corrected version of your code:\n\n```vba\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsSource As Worksheet\n    Dim wsDest As Worksheet\n    Dim newSheet As Worksheet\n    \n    Set wsSource = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Data_Input\")\n    \n    ' Check if the destination sheet exists\n    On Error Resume Next\n    Set wsDest = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Report\")\n    On Error GoTo",
